  "verbalization": "Alitretinoin, a retinoid compound, is shown to have a target relationship with HO-1-N-1 through multiple pathways, all of which involve the same intermediate molecule, 3-[2-[4-[5-[2-(2,3-Dihydroxyphenyl)ethyl]-2-hydroxyphenoxy]phenyl]ethyl]benzene-1,2-diol. This molecule is identified as a target of alitretinoin, OC-314, and S-117, and all three are linked to HO-1-N-1. The evidence suggests that alitretinoin exerts its biological effect by inhibiting the activity of this intermediate, which in turn leads to the activation of HO-1-N-1. The consistent presence of this intermediate across different targets implies a shared mechanism of action, likely involving the modulation of a common biochemical pathway. The high scores in the final scores indicate a strong and reliable relationship, supported by multiple independent pathways. The mechanism is thus supported by the presence of a common target molecule and the consistent evidence across different targets, reinforcing the hypothesis that alitretinoin interacts with HO-1-N-1 through this intermediate.",
